WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.501
  - If you're watching this,

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.337
 then you know by now a huge
 problem is heading our way.

00:00:03.337 --> 00:00:04.379
 An emergency meeting
 is being called.

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:06.256
 Our usual place immediately.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:07.090
 Free bagels.

00:00:08.217 --> 00:00:09.676
(dramatic music)

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.595
I've made a shocking discovery.

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:12.930
 (typing)
 (phone rings)

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.848
 I need you to get me in
 touch with NASA immediately.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.933
- Well, NASA and I aren't really

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:17.726
 on speaking terms these days.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.728
- Well, that'll change.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.356
  When you tell them that
  the moon is out of orbit.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:26.485
(dramatic music)

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:28.612
 - There's no need to panic.

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:30.155
- I'm not crazy!

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:31.949
(dramatic music)
(explosions)

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.368
 - Why are they lying
 about all this?

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:35.702
 - [Holdenfield] It's
 too late to stop.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.788
(dramatic flare)

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:40.707
- You knew all this was
happening before NASA.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.125
 - You're the
 unidentified source?

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.210
  - Oh, yes.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.671
 (extravagant music)

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:47.839
 - We're dealing with
 an intelligent entity.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.677
We're planning a mission
to attack this thing.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:53.220
 I'm asking you for your help.

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:55.722
  - Say yes, Brian.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.267
(blaring guitar)

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.518
  - I need you to be brave.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.982
 - If the moon really is what
 you think it is, suit up.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:08.694
 ♪ I see the bad moon arising ♪

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:10.279
 - [Man in space station] You
 have got a big gravity wave

00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:11.113
coming your way.

00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.781
You have to launch now!

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.032
  - Did he say gravity wave?

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:14.992
 (beep)

00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:17.661
 ♪ I see trouble on the way ♪

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:19.079
  - We're under water, guys!

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.710
 Uh... That's crazy.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.712
 (blaring instrumental)

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:30.048
 ♪ I hear hurricanes
 are blowing ♪

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:30.924
  - Whoa! Slow down!

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:32.801
 Whoo!

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:35.887
 - [Jocinda] What's the plan?

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:36.805
  - [Brian] Save the
  moon, save earth.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.517
 - Brian, what are you doing!?

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.185
 - It's flying itself!

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.646
 Wait for it.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:48.775
  (guns clicking into place)

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.818
  Let's go, you son of a...

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:50.819
(lasers)

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.321
 ♪ Don't go around tonight ♪

00:01:52.321 --> 00:01:53.655
 - Yes!

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:54.906
 ♪ Well it's bound
 to take your life ♪

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.450
  - Hang on!

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.492
  - Hang on!

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.910
 - Everybody, hang on!

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.746
 - We're going to get you home.

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:05.751
  ♪ There's a bad
  moon on the rise ♪

00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:10.047
 (camera click)
 (sirens)

00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:11.256
- It's on airplane mode.

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:15.135
 ♪ Looks like we're in
 for nasty weather ♪

